  "rule": "From the frozen 2026-10-17 catalog retain the same 70 eligible stable main-project releases in 45 MAJOR.MINOR families and the existing three documented mainline exclusions. Use the first eligible stable release in each family. Require every MAJOR.0 family from 10 through 33 (24 anchors, including 13.0.1 because ambiguous 13.0 is excluded), preserving the fixed oldest 10.0 and latest 33.7.2 endpoints. The latest endpoint is the sole exception to the first-release representative rule and does not count as an optional addition. Fill five remaining slots greedily: splitting a calendar gap into L and R days reduces the sum of squared gaps by 2*L*R. Choose the greatest reduction, then the earlier UTC calendar date, then numeric version. Keep every selected gap at least 60 calendar days and permit at most two optional minor-family additions in any major. Each selected family appears once. This balances major-history coverage and calendar spacing; it does not require an omitted numeric tag between every pair or claim a globally optimal calendar design. Use plain Maven artifacts before 23.1 and JRE artifacts thereafter. Selection reads no graphs, clusters, quality values or structural-change outcomes.",
